{
 "residual_definition": {
  "gimap_minimises": "scipy.optimize.least_squares(loss='soft_l1', f_scale=2.0) over the ring points i: cost = sum_i f^2 (sqrt(1 + r_i^2 / f^2) - 1), f = 2 px (r_i^2/2 for |r_i| << 2 px, f |r_i| for |r_i| >> 2 px); free: beam x, y, L, rot1, rot2 (tilt_fit.fit_tilted_geometry). Before it, the centre and L alone are fitted to ring pixels with the untilted residual (Physics and Methods 3.3, eq. 3.8) and the same loss.",
  "gimap_residual": "r_i = L (tan 2theta_i - tan 2theta_ring(i)) / pbar, in pixels: L the distance from the sample to the direct beam (m), 2theta_i the scattering angle of point i for the trial geometry (beam centre, L, rot1, rot2; GIMaP's lab_rays, pyFAI's rotation convention, rot3 fixed), 2theta_ring from q = 2 pi n / 58.38 A and lambda, pbar = (pixel_x + pixel_y)/2. Untilted, r_i is the radial pixel distance of the point from its ring. (tilt_fit.tilt_residual)",
  "gimap_points": "one point per azimuthal sector (about 2 px of arc, 36-720 a ring) of each matched ring: the intensity-weighted mean position of the valid pixels within +-max(3, min(10, 1.2 % of the radius)) px of the ring (first pass: twice this half-width h). Weights are measured detector intensity above the sector's lower quartile. Each sector must have valid pixels at radial offsets <= -h+1 and >= h-1 px. Its brightest pixel must stand above the quartile by at least 0.3 of the median such height among sectors that cover both flanks; points taken again about the tilted rings, 4 passes at most (tilt_fit.tilted_ring_points, refine_tilt)",
  "gimap_bounds": "beam centre within 4 % of the larger image side (12-60 px) of the start, L within +-25 % (and the user's range), |rot1|, |rot2| <= 30 deg",
  "gimap_sigma_reported": "4 or more contributing rings: jackknife over rings, sigma^2 = (n-1)/n sum_k (theta_(k) - mean)^2, theta_(k) the same robust fit with ring k left out (unbounded, from the full fit, same points); 2 rings: s^2 (J^T J)^-1, s^2 = sum r_i^2 / (N - p), forward-difference J (optimizer.estimate_uncertainty). With 3 rings and fitted tilts the jackknife refits all five parameters if every fit converges, with |rot1| and |rot2| < 30 deg, L in (0.75 L_full, 1.25 L_full) and s_min/s_max > sqrt(machine epsilon) for the Jacobian with unit-length columns. Otherwise all two-ring refits hold both tilts at their full-fit values. In this fallback the tilt errors come from the full five-parameter covariance, and x, y and L take the larger of the conditional jackknife and covariance errors. With tilt fixed by the user use the jackknife for x, y and L.",
  "pyfai_minimises": "sum_i (2theta_i - 2theta_ring(i))^2 in radians, plain least squares (GeometryRefinement.residu2; curve_fit = Levenberg-Marquardt); its sigma is curve_fit's s^2 (J^T J)^-1"
 },
